# Japanese study in Learn (14 October 2026)

- Open Learn, Japanese, Parcours. Review the due examples, or inspect a card and start its validated oral lesson. Corpus remains the searchable reference library; the page never calls an LLM. (14 October 2026)
- Existing personal history stays in Memory/Japanese/Japanese1.md. A web exposure or oral self-assessment appends a dated section there; DrillTracker.md and Site/study.json carry the resulting revision state. A new lesson also updates Site/japanese.json. One guarded Memory commit saves all affected files. (14 October 2026)
- Parameters live in src/learn/japaneseStudyModel.js. The page exposes reading size and lesson/review batch sizes. Successful red examples become orange for two days, then green for five days; two green successes become acquired examples. A diagnostic can reopen an already known prerequisite without declaring mastery, and a later failed review revokes the diagnostic result. (14 October 2026)
- Every teaching card must retain its exact SHA256, two distinct review identities, HTTPS evidence and no unresolved finding. The browser checks before teaching/export; the server checks again before writing learner state. Reference dictionaries, community sentences and external lessons never gain an invented approval. (14 October 2026)
- The web grades are explicitly oral self-assessments. No speech transcription, native certification or exhaustive grammar mastery is implied. Japanese/CLAUDE.md routes to the existing teaching rules; the japanese-context skill queries the local SQLite corpus and reads only relevant chronological sections. (14 October 2026)
- The corpus currently has 157 grammar cards, including 31 editorial N1 estimates, and 88 Japan cards. It is not a complete N1 course. The coverage page makes counts and missing competencies visible and stores research requests. (14 October 2026)
- Additional navigation data indexes 72 original Irodori lessons with PDF/audio links across four producer parts, A1 to A2/B1. Textbooks and audio stay on the Japan Foundation website. The local fetcher verifies 18 numbered lessons and a PDF/audio link in each part; no JLPT equivalence is assigned. (14 October 2026)
- Focused checks: vitest run src/learn server/japanese.test.js server/_cloudflare-adapter.test.js. The isolated browser proof uses the actual Japanese component and current records; it writes only fixture learner state. Production verification initializes preferences and reads them back, without fabricating a learning session. (14 October 2026)
- The history reader invalidates its cache after a confirmed write and reads the pinned Memory commit. A new lesson becomes visible immediately in the historical lessons tab, without depending on raw-file CDN expiry. (14 October 2026)

## Version 1.0.0 (15 October 2026)

- Learn > Japanese > Parcours now exposes a versioned usage guide. Its central configuration is src/learn/data/JapaneseRelease.json. Start with due oral reviews, select a level, study one unlocked point, reveal and compare the reference, then report the actual result. The diagnostic opens known prerequisites without declaring mastery. (15 October 2026)
- A newly approved revision can restart as a fresh exposure or diagnostic. Its earlier mastery is suspended, never transferred to different content. The original chronological history remains append-only. (15 October 2026)
- Coverage reads Memory/Japanese/Site/corpus/coverage.json only when its release matches the loaded catalogue. Invalid or unavailable evidence shows an explicit note; it is neither cached as success nor converted into zero coverage. The detailed open-point links remain visible. (15 October 2026)
- Release data: 439 independently reviewed editorial cards, 345 grammar cards (N5 168, N4 40, N3 48, N2 48, N1 41), two beyond-N1 pragmatics cards and 88 Japan cards. The complete corpus has 276244 records, including reference dictionaries and community sentences. N5 semantic audit currently proves 88 of 132 publisher points, with 44 open. Adding the last 18 approved cards does not silently claim new semantic coverage; unchanged bindings retain exact historical review evidence. (15 October 2026)
- Version 1.0.0 describes the usable application and reviewed corpus snapshot. Complete N5-to-N1 and beyond coverage, advanced comprehension and human/native certification are not release claims. Continue the named research gaps through Projects/zenray-japanese/ResumeCorpus.md. (15 October 2026)
- Focused release tests cover stale-content restart, exact-release coverage, failed-response retry, immutable lesson hashes, learner writes, duplicate events and concurrent commits. Production checks remain read-only and never fabricate study results. (15 October 2026)

